This repository contains code under different terms. Each part keeps the terms of its authors.

1. OSCA, FLOS and the V6Z80P software - Phil Ruston
   ------------------------------------------------
   The OSCA FPGA architecture, the FLOS operating system and the V6Z80P software are copyright (c) Phil Ruston
   2008-2012 (https://github.com/minexew/v6z80p, "Documentation/Credits & Disclaimers.txt"):

     "The V6Z80P PCB design, OSCA FPGA architecture, FLOS operating system and software supplied remain the
      copyright of Phil Ruston 2008-2012, but can be modified if desired and used freely for non-profit,
      non-commercial applications."

   This covers in this repository:
   - src/rtl/soc/osca_core.v, src/sim/ref_overrides/osca_core.v, src/rtl/prims/ and the other Verilog generated
     from the OSCA schematics (src/scripts/sch2v/), including their modified versions;
   - src/roms/FLOSv614.OSF and src/roms/boot_rom_mcu.bin (the OSCA boot ROM with a replaced tail);
   - the parts of the V6Z80P software used by the tests and the simulation images;
   - the SD card image attached to the releases (the programs, demos, tunes and pictures in it remain the
     property of their authors).
   These parts, and the bitstreams and core files (*.bin, *.kg) built from them, may be used for non-profit,
   non-commercial purposes only.

